# repeat(@posedge) inside a task causes incorrect timing on second call

- Source URL: https://github.com/verilator/verilator/issues/6593

When using repeat(N) @(posedge CLK); inside a task, Verilator produces incorrect timing behavior only on the second call of the task.


Verilator 5.041 devel rev v5.040-333-gd864057a6

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
```
`timescale 1ns/1ps
`default_nettype none

module tb();

  // VCD or FST Dump
  initial
    if( $test$plusargs ("WAVE") ) begin
      $dumpfile("wave_test1.dump");
      $dumpvars(0, tb);
    end

  parameter int PREOD = 100;          // 100ns(10MHz)

  bit CLK;

  localparam int H_PREOD = PREOD / 2;
  always #H_PREOD
    CLK = ~CLK;


  task automatic next_bit();    // NG
    repeat(4)
      @(posedge CLK);
  endtask

/*
  task automatic next_bit();    // OK
    repeat(3)
      @(posedge CLK);

    @(posedge CLK);
  endtask
*/

  bit [3:0] cnt = 0;

  task test_txd();
    cnt = 0;    
    next_bit();
    for(int i=0; i < 8; i++) begin
      ++cnt;
      next_bit();
    end

    ++cnt;
    next_bit();
  endtask


  initial begin
    test_txd();
    test_txd();

    repeat(10) @(posedge CLK);
    $finish;    
  end

endmodule
```
